# React Bits

**[React Bits](https://www.reactbits.dev/)** is an approved source for animated UI components, backgrounds, text effects, and related design patterns in Doxa—alongside shadcn/ui and Motion Primitives.

## Source of truth

- Catalog / docs: https://www.reactbits.dev/
- Installation: https://www.reactbits.dev/get-started/installation
- GitHub: https://github.com/DavidHDev/react-bits
- Prefer **TypeScript + Tailwind** variants (`TS` / `TW`) to match this repo.

## How to add a component

1. Prefer the shadcn CLI (owned source copied into the repo). Use the command from the component’s docs page, or the free-registry form:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add https://reactbits.dev/r/<ComponentName>-TS-TW
```

Example: `npx shadcn@latest add https://reactbits.dev/r/SplitText-TS-TW`

2. Or copy from the component Code tab (stack: TypeScript + Tailwind) into [`components/react-bits/`](components/react-bits/).

Install any peer deps listed on that page (`gsap`, `three`, etc.) only when the chosen component needs them.

## Conventions

- Keep copied components under `components/react-bits/` (or the path the CLI writes—then relocate there if it lands elsewhere).
- Customize copied source to match Doxa tokens (`app/globals.css`, neumorphic panel language)—same ownership model as shadcn under `components/ui/`.
- Use existing `cn` from `@/lib/utils`; do not add a second utils helper for React Bits components.
- Prefer purposeful motion that supports hierarchy and presence. Avoid decorative noise, endless loops on dense admin surfaces, and purple/glow demos that fight the design system.
- **Compose, don’t replace:**
  - shadcn/ui — default for non-animated primitives (Button, Dialog, forms, etc.)
  - Motion Primitives — preferred for focused motion primitives already covered there
  - React Bits — creative animations, backgrounds, and text effects when they fit the surface
- **Do not** suggest React Bits Pro (`@reactbits-pro/...`) unless the project has an active Pro license configured.

## When not to use it

- Pipeline / agents / Supabase Edge / workers — no UI animation stack there.
- Data-heavy tables and critical admin workflows — keep motion minimal or none.
- Prefer Motion Primitives when that catalog already covers the interaction (text effect, in-view reveal, spotlight, tilt, etc.).
